      "license": "MIT",
      "notes": [
        "The form.contact configuration opts into the public Form composition=contact API. Its consumer-owned onSubmit promise controls the send; the package implements no endpoint, transport or persistence.",
        "Fields compose the native Field, TextField, Textarea and Select components; submit binds to a native Button in the actions region. The error-summary uses errors and errorSummaryMessage, while host-authored success and error regions render through Banner after the submit promise resolves or rejects. Rejected submits retain the field values.",
        "Honeypot and Turnstile regions pass through consumer-owned host nodes. They do not create anti-abuse services, tokens or verification behavior. The runtime adapter resolves live nodes and the submit callback through sectionHosts[\"sections.form\"].",
        "Form is the public block anchor, not a claim that the components.form leaf is adopted. Source declarations do not qualify a consumer handler or consent host.",
        "Source-only import and token-read measurements are lower bounds; shared anatomy, accessibility, contrast and consumer runtime conformance remain unmeasured. Content bindings describe host adaptation points, not type-equivalent converters."
      ],
